Third-party content bundled in data/rules.json
----------------------------------------------
The file data/rules.json contains text and code examples from the
SEI CERT C Coding Standard and the SEI CERT C++ Coding Standard.

  Source:   https://github.com/cmu-sei/secure-coding-standards
  Commit:   73ee7a0dbe778512ba57a5f5ee0017af0ea09239
  Browsable: https://cmu-sei.github.io/secure-coding-standards/

  (c) 2026 Carnegie Mellon University.

  The SEI CERT Coding Standards text is licensed under the Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0):
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  The code examples contained in the standards are licensed under the MIT
  license: https://opensource.org/license/mit

Changes made: the Markdown source was parsed into a JSON structure; links
were reduced to text where they pointed into the standard's own site, HTML table markup was removed, and the examples were
paired (noncompliant with compliant). No rule wording was changed.
Rule IDs, titles and risk assessments are reproduced as published.

